ary fruit  that hasn't awakened for centuries means  that it is likely directly related to  joy boy and nika and i think that in  order to better understand how luffy's  new power could directly connect to two  legendary ancient figures like joy boy  nica we need to go back to the beginning  and by that i don't mean the voice entry  but even before the void century we need  to go back to over 1 100 years ago in  the world of one piece to the advanced  civilization that inhabited the moon the  same civilization whose descendants are  the modern day skypeans shandorians or  shandians and the beer [ __ ] but to find  the answers we need we first need to go  back 3500 years in our own world and  take a look at the olmec civilization of  mesoamerica now it is pretty clear that  the ancient civilization on the moon  along with all of their descendant  civilizations are heavily inspired by  ancient mesoamerican civilizations  including the aztecs and the mayans  the parallels are blatantly clear when  we look at the architecture art and  culture of these civilizations in one  piece and then compare them to the  real-life mesoamerican civilizations i  mean this particular statue of  quetzalcoatl the feathered serpent god  from aztec religion seems to have been  directly taken from real life and drawn  into one piece but while i've seen a lot  of talk about the sky civilizations  being inspired by the aztecs and mayans  i rarely hear talk about the olmecs who  predate the aztecs and mayans and  without whom the aztecs and mayans and  other mesoamerican civilizations would  not have existed the olmec are  considered to be the first major  civilization of ancient mexico and their  history dates all the way back to 1500  bc this is of course many centuries  before the aztec and mine empires would  flourish in mesoamerica it is believed  that the olmec civilization pioneered  many of the things that later  mesoamerican civilizations would become  known for including that famous mayan  calendar the ball games that the  mesoamerican people played and even the  gods that they worshipped it can all be  traced back to the olmecs so the olmecs  could be seen as the ancestors of the  mayans and aztecs just like the moon  civilization is the ancestor  civilization of the shandorians skypians  and beer cuts but here's the crazy thing  about the olmec people the name olmec  literally means the rubber people  because they lived in an area that was  known for producing rubber now olmec is  not what the people call themselves we  don't know what they call themselves but  this is the name given to them because  of the rubber producing area that they  inhabited the olmecs did not leave  behind any written history or oral  traditions so everything we know about  them comes from artifacts and from the  influence that their civilization had on  other civilizations that came later if  this gives you the same vibes as the  moon civilization and the void century  trust me you're not the only one the  olmecs are probably best known for  creating giant head statues some of  which are over 3 meters in height in  other words these stone heads are just  big enough for a certain giant straw hat  to fit them and speaking of giants the  jaguar is a very important sacred animal  in mesoamerica so it is possible that  the giant jaguar d saul will turn out to  be more important than we even realize  now many people have heard about the  aztec god quetzalcoatl who often takes  the shape of a feathered serpent some  have discussed the potential connection  between luffy and quetzalcoatl in the  past especially because quetzalcoatl was  the god of the sun and of the dawn as  well as the winds and the sky nika of  course is the sun god joy boy and luffy  are going to bring about a new dawn so  quetzalcoatl the feathered serpent may  be an even better fit for luffy's  hypothetical mythical zone devil fruit  than the monkey king sun wukong but most  people don't realize that this divine  feathered serpent that the aztecs  worshiped as quettal koatl actually  originated with the olmecs the olmecs  the rubber people also worshipped a  feathered serpent deity if the sky races  represent the newer civilizations such  as the aztecs and mayans then the moon  civilization represents the olmecs and  so the truth about nika joyboy and the  true nature of luffy's legendary devil  fruit may lead all the way back to the  moon itself now i'm not saying this will  happen because we already have two major  dragons in wano but it would be pretty  insane to see kaido's dragon having to  face luffy's feathered serpent form with  like burning rubber all over his body  anyway the similarities between nika  joyboy and the feathered serpent deity  that came to be known as quetzalcoatl  don't end there the rulers of ancient  mesoamerica would often equate  themselves with quetzalcoatl implying  that they were his current incarnation  or reincarnation on earth the aztec  people believed that quetzalcoatl would  one day return to earth and according to  some historical sources when hernan  cortes and the conquistadors landed in  america in 1519 aztec emperor montezuma  ii believed that cortes was actually  quetzalcoatl returning to claim his  throne whether this is true is actually  still disputed by historians but this  idea of quetzalcoatl being incarnated in  different rulers and returning to earth  to claim his throne definitely gives off  strong joy boy and nika energy side note  but gone fall and his armor seem to be a  direct reference to spanish  conquistadors which again stresses the  parallels between mesoamerica and the  sky people even in terms of his  personality what we know about  quetzalcoatl echoes what we know about  joy boy and nika although in modern  western culture serpents are often  associated with sinister things  quetzalcoatl was actually a kind and  gentle deity and he did not want to harm  any living creature he was a benefactor  of mankind and he gifted them incredibly  valuable knowledge including things like  farming medicine and other important  crafts he was loved by the people and he  brought them joy oh and if you're  looking for a monkey connection in his  form as ehekar he is the wind and he is  represented by spider monkeys among  other creatures so if the key to luffy's  new transformation and the ending of one  piece itself lies with the olmecs and  their mesoamerican descendants do we  have any clues about what luffy's new  powers could be well right off the bat  shape-shifting is a very popular power  among mesoamerican gods including  quetzalcoatl and since he can take the  form of a giant feathered serpent he can  also fly and his powers are associated  with the sun the sky and wind that of  course gives us many options to  speculate about in terms of the direct  rubber connection the ancient  mesoamericans were the first people to  invent rubber balls and they were a very  important part of their culture these  rubber balls could be used for playing  ball games or as important religious  offerings among other uses another aztec  god who represents the morning star  venus and whose name can be translated  as dawn lord or lord of the dawn is  associated with powerful rays that are  able to hurt people and crops the  interesting thing about this deity is  that there is a known image of him  burning a rubber ball so again that  whole burning rubber and melting rubber  aspect could come into play also you  might have noticed that i didn't tell  you this deity's name so i guess i have  to do that now  his name is tlauis kalpatikutli  now it is important to mention that to  both the aztecs and the maya the rubber  latex that flowed from the tree  represented blood and semen rubber was  symbolic of fertility of new life and it  was often burned buried or laid in  sacrificial pools as an offering to  deities now i don't think that luffy's  power will be related to that other  thing but something associated with  blood could be a part of the equation  bloodletting played a massively  important part in mesoamerican religions  and luffy has already used a form of  blood manipulation as far back as gear  2. he has also used air manipulation to  blow air into his own body so that wind  and air connection to quetzalcoatl could  also come into play all in all i think  that there are many fascinating theories  regarding luffy's new forms and powers  and his connection to joy boy i'm a fan  of many of them but i don't think we can  underestimate the importance of the  rubber people the olmecs and all the  other mesoamerican connections to the  ancient kingdom the void century and the  civilization on the moon joy boy nika  the gomu gomi and the one piece itself  are all going to take us back to the  ancient kingdom and the best clues that  we have about the true nature of that  kingdom are the real life kingdoms that  inspired it let me know what you guys  think about luffy's new transformation  what is his connection to joy boy and  nika is he inheriting this divine will  is he himself a reincarnation of this  legendary warrior or is something else  going on then of course what new powers  do you think luffy is about to unlock  are we talking awakened gomugamunomi a  completely new element like fire or lava  or does he actually possess a mythical  zone fruit like the sunbu kung fruit or  the feathered serpent fruit don't forget  to leave your feedback down in the  comments below if you guys enjoyed this  one piece video and you want to see more  in the future leave a quick like and  comment it only takes a second but it  helps a lot and remember that  subscribing and hitting that  notification bell is a very real and  completely free way of supporting the  channel you can also hit me up on  twitter and instagram at animeopror as  always thank you guys so much for  watching and until next time see ya  space cowboys
 

